workflows.prompt:
Edit this real-estate listing photo. Improve ONLY its technical photographic quality, like a professional retoucher making a faithful correction:
- correct the exposure: brighten dark areas naturally and recover blown-out highlights where possible;
- set a neutral white balance (remove colour casts) with natural colours;
- straighten the image so that vertical lines (walls, door frames, windows, furniture edges) are truly vertical;
- reduce noise and improve sharpness and clarity.

STRICT RULES — the result must show exactly the same place:
- do NOT add, remove, move or replace any object, furniture, decoration, person or animal;
- do NOT change materials, wall colours, floors, tiles or textures;
- do NOT invent or change what is visible through windows or doors; keep blinds and curtains exactly as they are;
- do NOT repair, hide or clean damage, stains, cracks, dirt or clutter;
- do NOT change the room geometry, size or proportions; keep the same framing and aspect ratio;
- keep any text, logos and watermarks unchanged.

The output must be a photorealistic photograph, not an illustration.

